      "writtenOn": "2019-07-12T21:27:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e\u003eOn start-up, we should make EC query all TCPCs to get all live data and cache them. If product_id doesn\u0027t match the hard-coded value, the live data should precede. If EC fails to get a live data, it should populate the cache with a hardcoded value.\n\nIf the live data precedes the hard-coded when the product_id does not match, then depthcharge will not be able to identify the chip when the FW is bad/corrupt. Also to maintain the backwards compatibility, renew \u003d 0 will return hardcoded value(before update) and renew \u003d 1 will return live data(after update).\n\nI am not sure if you are looking for a response for anything specific in that comment.",
      "parentUuid": "0c9d02e2_01076ed5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5161,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 5165,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "3336354e62a7380603febbe1ba24bb55e718e8d1",
